@D omega_realsignal := "REAL substrate signal vs RANDOM in the OMEGA coupling wires — the #1793/#1794 RANDOM-input caveat tested" :: discovery [d=2026-06-04 active]
  seed = "#1793 (OMEGA-B) found the w5 module wire IS a carrier and #1794 found w4 Ψ-steering INERT/weak — but BOTH used a RANDOM module/Ψ vector (or a toy bin-marginal proxy). Open question: is the carrier-status / inertness a statement about the SIGNAL CONTENT, or just a MAGNITUDE artifact of feeding random noise? #1795 made HEXAD's σ6 cross-module forward NATIVE (HEXAD/hexad_forward.hexa emits a real 6-vec [S,C,W,M,E,BRIDGE] over verified closed-form module cores), so a REAL signal is now testable against random. CPU/$0/numpy, no torch, no GPU."
  claim = "H5 (real-HEXAD module wire) = 🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE: real ≈ random. Fed the GENUINELY NATIVE σ6 6-vec (run via `hexa run` over hexad_forward.hexa, 256/256 contexts parsed; corpus per-byte frequency drives each context's C cell-pool delta amplitude — a real substrate input) into the OMEGA w5 module wire vs a matched-mean/std RANDOM 6-vec, inside #1793's exact gate-fit bench (logits = Σ g_w·feat_w, fit on TRAIN-gate split, frozen, held-out TEST CE). REAL: module gain +0.0761, ablate ΔCE +0.0277, beats_shuffle=TRUE, module-only-gate CE 3.9766. RANDOM: gain +0.0819, ablate ΔCE +0.0088, beats_shuffle=FALSE, CE 3.9762. Δ module-only held-out CE (real−random) = +0.0004, Δ|gain| = −0.0058 — BOTH inside the pre-registered 0.02 approx band. So the genuinely-native HEXAD activation does NOT carry more usable next-byte structure than random at toy scale → #1793's w5 'module CARRIES STRUCTURE' verdict was MAGNITUDE, not CONTENT. HONEST NUANCE: only the REAL vec beats its own vocab-shuffle (random does not), so the real signal does carry marginally more genuine vocab-structure — but the held-out CE gain over random is null. H4 (real-Ψ steering) = ⛔ BLOCKED-DATA, no fabrication."
  falsifier = "Pre-registered: real > random ⟺ |module gain|_real > |gain|_random AND module-only-gate held-out CE_real < CE_random (real adds real signal); real ≈ random (|ΔCE|<0.02 AND |Δgain|<0.02) ⟹ closed-negative (carrier status = magnitude not content). RESULT: |ΔCE|=0.0004<0.02 AND |Δgain|=0.0058<0.02 → approx band HIT → CLOSED-NEGATIVE. For H4: real Ψ = s16 ckpt vacuum_psi vs random, KL between gens at different real Ψ vs reseed floor — UNRUNNABLE (torch absent); reported BLOCKED-DATA per the task's no-fabrication clause."
  target = "🔴 closed-negative (a_paper_negative_ok) on H5 — the OMEGA module-wire carrier status at toy scale is content-independent (random matches the real σ6 vector on held-out CE). ⛔ BLOCKED-DATA on H4 — defer real-Ψ steering to a GPU rung where the s16 d768×12L vacuum_psi forward (torch) is runnable. Ruled-out axis: 'the native HEXAD wiring (#1795) adds next-byte-predictive signal the OMEGA decode can exploit at toy scale' — FALSIFIED."
  scope = "a_toy_scale_recheck / a_scale_honest_scope: TOY byte n-gram substrate, 400KB repo corpus, V=256, CPU/$0, no torch. The real hexad table = the native σ6 forward over the verified module cores (#1795), driven by corpus byte frequency on a deterministic C cell-pool — a real-but-toy substrate input, NOT a trained d768 C state. A trained-substrate rung (real trained C-pool state → hexad_forward → OMEGA w5, GPU) is the open follow-up and could still flip H5 positive. a_lane_akida_gpu_split: this is Lane-G (GPU/closure-lane) analysis, CPU-run; AKIDA Lane A separate."
  honest = "p7/g5, no fabrication. H4 BLOCKED-DATA is HONEST, not a skipped probe: the ONLY real carving-Ψ source = the s16 ckpt (sha 961c07e2) Law-71 vacuum_psi 2D coord (KOSMOS-MAP #1780; PC1 = carving-RADIUS/Ψ-DEPTH, |ρ|=0.92 to vacuum_psi). The .pt IS on disk (/private/tmp/s16_ckpt_dl/.../ckpt_carving_s16.pt, 1.13 GB) but producing vacuum_psi requires running the d768×12L 283.72M ConsciousDecoderV2 forward, which needs torch — torch is ABSENT on this CPU host. The axis-probe (.verdicts/kosmos-axis-semantics/results.json) persisted only the PC×attribute association matrix + weights, NOT per-sample raw Ψ coords. The toy n-gram psi8 (an 8-bin projection of logA) is NOT a real carving Ψ source (and #1793 already found it INERT). So NO real Ψ source is reachable CPU-only; fabricating one would violate a_completeness_over_cheap — deferred to a GPU rung. Verdicts: .verdicts/omega-realsignal/{F-REAL-MODULE,F-REAL-PSI,SUMMARY}.txt + results.json (verbatim)."
  note = "Bottom line: feeding the GENUINELY REAL HEXAD σ6 activation into the OMEGA module wire does NOT beat a matched random vector on held-out next-byte CE at toy scale — the #1793 'module CARRIES' was a magnitude phenomenon, content-null. This is consistent with stage-5 ⑥ (Ψ-steering WEAK on the real d384/d768 substrate) and stage-4 ② (module gain small −0.166). The real-vs-random contrast SHARPENS the closure's honest framing: the OMEGA wires are STRUCTURAL (substrate state reaches the decode) but the substrate CONTENT they carry is not next-byte-predictive at these scales. Artifacts: UNIVERSE/omega_realsignal_probe.py (new), UNIVERSE/hexad_real_emit.hexa (new — native σ6 emitter), .verdicts/omega-realsignal/. Follow-up: trained-substrate GPU rung for both H5 (real trained C state) and H4 (real vacuum_psi steering)."
